<tspan x="36" y="35"></tspan><tspan x="36" y="49"></tspan><tspan x="36" y="63">MWM</tspan></text></switch></g></g></g><g data-cell-id="u1n8Xw_qIOu34VLNSmKq-13"><g transform="translate(0.5,0.5)"><path d="M 235.71 38.82 L 353.63 38.82" fill="none" stroke="#000000" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-dasharray="3 3" pointer-events="stroke" style="stroke: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000);"></path><path d="M 358.88 38.82 L 351.88 42.32 L 353.63 38.82 L 351.88 35.32 Z" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-miterlimit="10" pointer-events="all" style="fill: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000); stroke: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000);"></path></g></g><g data-cell-id="u1n8Xw_qIOu34VLNSmKq-7"><g transform="translate(0.5,0.5)"><ellipse cx="199.29" cy="38.82" rx="36.43" ry="17.65" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000" stroke-dasharray="3 3" pointer-events="all" style="fill: var(--ge-adaptive-bg, #ffffff); stroke: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000);"></ellipse></g></g><g data-cell-id="u1n8Xw_qIOu34VLNSmKq-8"><g transform="translate(0.5,0.5)"><ellipse cx="396.43" cy="38.82" rx="36.43" ry="17.65" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000" stroke-dasharray="3 3" pointer-events="all" style="fill: var(--ge-adaptive-bg, #ffffff); stroke: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000);"></ellipse></g></g><g data-cell-id="u1n8Xw_qIOu34VLNSmKq-10"><g><rect x="162.86" y="63.53" width="72.86" height="35.29" fill="none" stroke="none" pointer-events="all"></rect></g><g><g><switch><foreignObject style="overflow: visible; text-align: left;" pointer-events="none" width="100%" height="100%" requiredFeatures="http://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/feature#Extensibility"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: flex; align-items: unsafe center; justify-content: unsafe center; width: 71px; height: 1px; padding-top: 81px; margin-left: 164px;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 0; text-align: center; color: #000000; "><div style="display: inline-block; font-size: 12px; font-family: Helvetica; color: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000); line-height: 1.2; pointer-events: all; white-space: normal; word-wrap: normal; ">mathematical<div>reality</div></div></div></div></foreignObject><text x="199" y="78" fill="#000000" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="12px" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000);"><tspan x="199" y="78">mathematical</tspan><tspan x="199" y="92">reality</tspan></text></switch></g></g></g><g data-cell-id="u1n8Xw_qIOu34VLNSmKq-11"><g><rect x="360" y="63.53" width="72.86" height="35.29" fill="none" stroke="none" pointer-events="all"></rect></g><g><g><switch><foreignObject style="overflow: visible; text-align: left;" pointer-events="none" width="100%" height="100%" requiredFeatures="http://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/feature#Extensibility"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: flex; align-items: unsafe center; justify-content: unsafe center; width: 71px; height: 1px; padding-top: 81px; margin-left: 361px;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 0; text-align: center; color: #000000; "><div style="display: inline-block; font-size: 12px; font-family: Helvetica; color: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000); line-height: 1.2; pointer-events: all; white-space: normal; word-wrap: normal; ">physical<div>reality</div></div></div></div></foreignObject><text x="396" y="78" fill="#000000" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="12px" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000);"><tspan x="396" y="78">physical</tspan><tspan x="396" y="92">reality</tspan></text></switch></g></g></g><g data-cell-id="u1n8Xw_qIOu34VLNSmKq-15"><g><rect x="72.86" y="35.29" width="42.86" height="21.18" fill="none" stroke="none" pointer-events="all"></rect></g><g><g><switch><foreignObject style="overflow: visible; text-align: left;" pointer-events="none" width="100%" height="100%" requiredFeatures="http://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/feature#Extensibility"><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="display: flex; align-items: unsafe center; justify-content: unsafe center; width: 41px; height: 1px; padding-top: 46px; margin-left: 74px;"><div style="box-sizing: border-box; font-size: 0; text-align: center; color: #000000; "><div style="display: inline-block; font-size: 12px; font-family: Helvetica; color: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000); line-height: 1.2; pointer-events: all; white-space: normal; word-wrap: normal; ">models</div></div></div></foreignObject><text x="94" y="49" fill="#000000" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="12px" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ge-adaptive-fg, #000000);">models</text></switch></g></g></g></g></g></g></g><switch><g requiredFeatures="http://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/feature#Extensibility"></g><a transform="translate(0,-5)" xlink:href="https://www.drawio.com/doc/faq/svg-export-text-problems" target="_blank"><text text-anchor="middle" font-size="10px" x="50%" y="100%">Text is not SVG - cannot display</text></a></switch></svg>
  </div>
  <p>
    MWM does not claim to model all of mathematics. It focuses specifically on the mathematics supporting <strong>mathematical physics</strong>, balancing two design parameters:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><em>What physical theories can be modeled?</em></li>
    <li><em>At what level of depth can the modeling mathematics be understood?</em></li>
  </ol><div>MWM expresses its concepts formally, embedded in natural language explanations, using single-sorted first-order logic and ZF set theory as its foundational baseline.<i></i></div>

  <h2>2. The Cornerstone Axiom, Ordinals, and Number Trees</h2>

  <p>
    MWM operates as an <strong>effective model</strong>: rather than building foundational set-theoretic proofs from scratch, it asserts established mathematical structures as governing axioms. The cornerstone axiom of MWM is:
  </p>

  <div class="axiom-box">
    <strong>(No(ε₀), +, ·) is a totally ordered algebraic field</strong>
  </div>

  <p>where:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The carrier set <code>No(ε₀)</code> consists of nodes on the <strong>2-successor number tree</strong> whose tree depth (birthday) is strictly less than the ordinal <code>ε₀</code>.</li>
    <li>The total order (<code>≤</code>) and the arithmetic operations (<code>+</code>, <code>·</code>) are defined recursively with respect to the node's stage of creation, i.e. it's birthday.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Because <code>No(ε₀)</code> is <strong>non-Archimedean</strong>, standard ε–δ analysis is set aside in favor of a <strong>constructive nonstandard analysis</strong>. <code>No(ε₀)</code> serves as the ambient field for all arithmetic and continuous modeling.
  </p><h3>the ordinals</h3><div>The class of ordinal numbers play an important role in modern mathematics. The ordinals model the concept of a collection of well ordered elements. Most graduates of a general education still model well ordered elements with perhaps the first mathematical model they encountered: the natural numbers. The ordinals provide a much more extensive model of order. However, like the cornerstone axiom, the ordinals will not be formally modeled; instead they are assumed to be mathematical fact. The natural language description is that the ordinals are the equivalence classes of isomorphic (set,&lt;<sub>w</sub>) pairs over the universe of sets &amp; their possible well orders, where the von Neumann ordinals are a canonical class of equivalence class instances consistent with ZF axioms.</div><div><br></div><div>The finite ordinals coincide with the natural numbers (as defined by finite induction). The ordinal ω is the supremum of the natural numbers, and the ordinal ε<sub>0</sub> is greater than ω+1.</div><h3>number trees</h3><div>MWM considers numbers to be the elements of sets defined by 2 and 4 successor inductive definitions whose inductive stages are indexed by the ordinals. As the elements of the set in the 2-successor case can be represented by a binary tree, the set is referred to as a number tree. John Conway was the first to describe recursive definitions for a total order among elements (nodes) of a number tree, as well as recursive definitions for adding and multiplying numbers. It is these recursive definitions that are referred to when denoting the totally ordered algebraic field as&nbsp;<b>No</b>(ε<sub>0</sub>), +, ·).</div>

  <h2>3. Key number tree number sets</h2>

  <p>Besides the set <b>No</b>(ε<sub>0</sub>), we want to define two other number tree sets. Let&nbsp;<b>No</b>(α), where α is an ordinal, denote the set of all number tree nodes whose birthday is less than α; then</p><ul><li><b>No</b>(ω)&nbsp; is the set of all finite ordinals, and</li><li><b>No</b>(ω+1) is {the set of all finite ordinals} union {the set of all number tree nodes whose birthday is ω}.</li></ul>We consider the commutative ring (<b>No</b>(ω), +, ·) where the operations are inherited from No(ε0).&nbsp; We demonstrate the isomorphism between (No(ω), +, ·) and (𝔻, +, ·) where elements of 𝔻 are dyadic rationals and operations on 𝔻 are those of dyadic arithmetic. 𝔻 becomes the arena of all numeric calculation in MWM. Thus numeric calculation occurs within the context of an Euclidean domain rather than a field.<div class="container"><br></div><div class="container">We don't consider any algebraic structure for which No(ω+1) is the carrier set. Instead we only use No(ω+1) as a source for the numbers that can be used in algebraic expressions, as part of a syntactic vocabulary. But we note that these numbers also exist in No(ε0), and so are elements of an algebraic field. We also note that x ∈ ℝ ⇒ x ∈ No(ω+1); however, there is no algebraic structure associated with No(ω+1) with which to compare to the Archimedean field (ℝ, +, ·). And we finally note that No(ω+1) includes elements not in ℝ. In particular No(ω+1) includes non-finite and infinitesimal numbers.<h2>4. The Precision Evaluation Function</h2>

  <p>
    To evaluate an algebraic expression <code>E</code> whose number terms belong to <code>No(ω+1)</code>, MWM defines a computable truncation map:
  </p>
  <div class="math-display">
    <code class="math-formula">eval(E, p)</code>
  </div>

  <p>Given a target precision <code>p ∈ ℕ</code>:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Each number node in <code>E</code> is replaced by its 2-successor tree address truncated to the first <code>p</code> directional choices, yielding an exact element of <code>𝔻</code>.</li>
    <li>Infinitesimal terms are bounded and resolved, reproducing the standard part map (<code>st</code>) of nonstandard analysis.</li>
    <li>The expression resolves to an expression whose number terms are dyadic rationals.</li>
  </ol><div>The following illustration summarises</div><div><div align="center" style="margin: 16px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" data-diagram-name="summary" style="background: transparent; color-scheme: light dark; cursor: pointer;" version="1.1" width="324px" height="519px" viewBox="0 0 324 519" id="ge-svg-GJ5roQyqgNA0ex0WR1U0" content="&lt;mxfile host=&quot;embed.diagrams.net&quot;&gt;&lt;diagram id=&quot;page-1&quot; name=&quot;Page-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/diagram&gt;&lt;/mxfile&gt;" title="Double-click to edit diagram in Draw.io"><style type="text/css">@supports (color: light-dark(#000, #fff)) { #ge-svg-GJ5roQyqgNA0ex0WR1U0 { --ge-adaptive-bg: light-dark(#ffffff, var(--ge-dark-color, #121212)); --ge-adaptive-fg: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff)); } }</style><defs><style xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" id="MJX-SVG-styles">
mjx-container[overflow="scroll"][display] {
  overflow: auto clip;
  min-width: initial !important;
}

mjx-container[overflow="truncate"][display] {
  overflow: hidden clip;
  min-width: initial !important;
}

mjx-container[display] {
  display: block;
  text-align: center;
  justify-content: center;
  margin: .7em 0;
  padding: .3em 2px;
}

mjx-container[display][width="full"] {
  display: flex;
}

mjx-container[justify="left"] {
  text-align: left;
  justify-content: left;
}

mjx-container[justify="right"] {
  text-align: right;
  justify-content: right;
}

mjx-container[jax="SVG"] {
  direction: ltr;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

mjx-container[jax="SVG"] &gt; svg {
  overflow: visible;
  min-height: 1px;
  min-width: 1px;
}

mjx-container[jax="SVG"] &gt; svg a {
  fill: blue;
  stroke: blue;
}

rect[data-sre-highlighter-added]:has(+ .mjx-selected), rect[data-sre-highlighter-bbox].mjx-selected {
  stroke: black;
  stroke-width: 80px;
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  rect[data-sre-highlighter-added]:has(+ .mjx-selected), rect[data-sre-highlighter-bbox].mjx-selected {
    stroke: #C8C8C8;
  }
}

mjx-container[jax="SVG"] mjx-break {
  white-space: normal;
  line-height: 0;
  clip-path: rect(0 0 0 0);
  font-family: MJX-ZERO ! important;
}

mjx-break[size="0"] {
  letter-spacing: -0.999em;
}

mjx-break[size="1"] {
  letter-spacing: -0.889em;
}

mjx-break[size="2"] {
  letter-spacing: -0.833em;
}

mjx-break[size="3"] {
  letter-spacing: -0.778em;
}

mjx-break[size="4"] {
  letter-spacing: -0.722em;
}

mjx-break[size="5"] {
  letter-spacing: -0.667em;
}

mjx-container[jax="SVG"] mjx-break[newline]::before {
  white-space: pre;
  content: "\A";
}

mjx-break[newline] + svg[width="0.054ex"] {
  margin-right: -1px;
}

mjx-break[prebreak] {
  letter-spacing: -.999em;
}

@font-face /* zero */ {
  font-family: MJX-ZERO;
  src: url(data:application/x-font-woff;charset=utf-8;base64,) format("woff");
}

g[data-mml-node="merror"] &gt; g {
  fill: red;
  stroke: red;
}

g[data-mml-node="merror"] &gt; rect[data-background] {
  fill: yellow;
  stroke: none;
}

g[data-mml-node="mtable"] &gt; line[data-line], svg[data-table] &gt; g &gt; line[data-line] {
  stroke-width: 70px;
  fill: none;
}

g[data-mml-node="mtable"] &gt; rect[data-frame], svg[data-table] &gt; g &gt; rect[data-frame] {
  stroke-width: 70px;
  fill: none;
}

g[data-mml-node="mtable"] &gt; .mjx-dashed, svg[data-table] &gt; g &gt; .mjx-dashed {
  stroke-dasharray: 140;
}

g[data-mml-node="mtable"] &gt; .mjx-dotted, svg[data-table] &gt; g &gt; .mjx-dotted {
  stroke-linecap: round;
  stroke-dasharray: 0,140;
}

g[data-mml-node="mtable"] &gt; g &gt; svg {
  overflow: visible;
}

[jax="SVG"] mjx-tool {
  display: inline-block;
  position: relative;
  width: 0;
  height: 0;
}

[jax="SVG"] mjx-tool &gt; mjx-tip {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
}

mjx-tool &gt; mjx-tip {
  display: inline-block;
  line-height: 0;
  padding: .2em;
  border: 1px solid #888;
  background-color: #F8F8F8;
  color: black;
  box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px #AAAAAA;
}

g[data-mml-node="maction"][data-toggle] {
  cursor: pointer;
}

mjx-status {
  display: block;
  position: fixed;
  left: 1em;
  bottom: 1em;
  min-width: 25%;
  padding: .2em .4em;
  border: 1px solid #888;
  font-size: 90%;
  background-color: #F8F8F8;
  color: black;
}

g[data-mjx-collapsed] {
  fill: #55F;
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) /* svg maction */ {
  mjx-tool &gt; mjx-tip {
    background-color: #303030;
      color: #E0E0E0;
      box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px #000;
  }
  mjx-status {
    background-color: #303030;
      color: #E0E0E0;
  }
  g[data-mjx-collapsed] {
    fill: #88F;
  }
}

foreignObject[data-mjx-xml] {
  font-family: initial;
  line-height: normal;
  overflow: visible;
}

foreignObject[data-mjx-html] {
  overflow: visible;
}

mjx-measure-xml {
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 0;
  display: inline-block;
  line-height: normal;
  white-space: normal;
}

mjx-html {
  display: inline-block;
  line-height: normal;
  text-align: initial;
  white-space: initial;
}

mjx-html-holder {
  display: block;
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  right: 0;
}

mjx-container[jax="SVG"] path[data-c], mjx-container[jax="SVG"] use[data-c] {
